msgid "The ``em`` API, essentials"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*What a plugin, a script and the console use to read and write a study: "
"the graph, the writes, the vocabularies, the application, and the context"
" of a plugin.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``em`` is the scripting API of the Extended Matrix, part of the s3Dgraphy"
" library: ``from s3dgraphy import em``. It has two halves. **The graph** "
"— reading, searching, writing, vocabularies, packages — is the same in "
"EMStudio, in EM Tools and in a script with no application. **The "
"application** — selection, views, the Space, commands — is given by the "
"program that hosts the code, and answers *no application* on the command "
"line. ``em.help()`` prints what is there; this page lists what a plugin "
"needs most. The version of the API is ``em.API_VERSION`` (``1.2.0`` in "
"EMStudio 1.6), which ``em_api_min`` in the envelope is read against."
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
msgid "The graph"
msgstr "Der Graph"

msgid "Call"
msgstr ""

msgid "What it gives"
msgstr ""

msgid "``em.graph``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The study open in EMStudio (or by ``em.open`` on the command line), read "
"again at every use."
msgstr ""

msgid "``em.graph.node(ref)``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A node by its id or by its name (an ambiguous name is refused with the "
"ids it names). ``em.graph.find(ref)`` gives ``None`` instead of a "
"refusal."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid "``em.graph.nodes(type=…, name=…, where={quale: value})``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The nodes of a type (``US``, ``extractor``, ``document``…), with a name, "
"whose properties match (a value or the address of a concept)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``em.graph.edges(source=…, target=…, type=…)``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The edges, filtered."
msgstr ""

msgid "``em.graph.chronology(ref=None)``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The chronology the core computes, nothing written."
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A node (``NodeView``) has ``id``, ``name``, ``type``, ``description``, "
"``data`` (read only), ``props()``, ``prop(name, default)`` (the value of "
"a property), ``property(name)``, ``edges(type=…, "
"direction=\"out\"|\"in\"|\"both\")`` and ``neighbours(type=…, "
"direction=…)``. A property (``PropertyView``) has ``value``, ``term`` "
"(``{concept, label, lang, vocabulary, version}`` for a controlled value),"
" ``unit`` and ``provenance`` (the ids it comes from)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Writing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"One block is **one act**: one step of ``Edit ▸ Undo``, one line in the "
"Log, and an act that records who wrote it — the person, and the plugin "
"when a plugin's command wrote it. The block is applied when it ends; an "
"error inside it applies nothing. There is no other way to change a study:"
" the views of the graph are read only."
msgstr ""

msgid "``tx.…``"
msgstr ""

msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

msgid "``add_node(node_type, name, id=…, description=…, data=…)``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A node of a type the core knows; its id, when not given, follows from the"
" act, so a script run twice adds nothing the second time."
msgstr ""

msgid "``update(node, field, value)``, ``clear(node, field)``"
msgstr ""

msgid "``name``, ``description``, or ``data.<key>``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``add_edge(source, edge_type, target)``, ``remove_edge(…)``, "
"``remove(node)``"
msgstr ""

msgid "Edges of the EM language, checked when the act ends."
msgstr ""

msgid "``set_property(unit, quale, value, concept=…, lang=…)``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The property of a unit, created when missing; with ``concept``, the "
"double value: the address of the concept and its label."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``add_extractor(kind, on=…, point=…)``, ``start_pose(set, on=…)``, "
"``compute(combiner_type, on=…)``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Extractors, landmark sets and combiners of a package, as the tools of the"
" Viewer place and compute them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``em.write(label, volatile=True)`` writes proposals that are drawn and "
"not saved (the capability ``ingest-batch``); ``dry_run=True`` makes the "
"act a proof: what it would write, nothing applied."
msgstr ""

msgid "Vocabularies and packages"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``em.vocab.find(uri)`` — a concept installed on this computer, or "
"``None``; ``concept.label(lang)``, ``concept.labels``, "
"``concept.broader``, ``concept.narrower``. ``em.vocab.search(text, "
"lang=…)``, ``em.vocab.installed()``."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``em.profiles.active()`` — the packages the open study uses; "
"``em.profiles.extractor_type(id)``, ``landmark_set(id)``, "
"``label(type_id, lang)``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The application"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``em.app.selection()``, ``em.app.select(ids)``, ``em.app.view(name)``, "
"``em.app.notify(message, level)``, ``em.app.space.camera()``, "
"``em.app.space.frame(ids)``, ``em.app.space.pick(prompt, primitive)``, "
"``em.app.commands.run(command_id, **slots)``. ``em.app.available`` is "
"``False`` with no application. ``em.host.current().language()`` is the "
"language of the interface."
msgstr ""

msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``em.on(event, fn)`` and, in a plugin, ``ctx.on(event, fn)``: "
"``fn(payload)`` runs after each ``selection-changed``, ``graph-changed``,"
" ``document-opened``, ``document-saved``, ``document-closed`` or "
"``locale-changed``."
msgstr ""

msgid "The context of a plugin"
msgstr ""

msgid "``setup(ctx)`` receives the context of the plugin:"
msgstr ""

msgid "``ctx.…``"
msgstr ""

msgid "What it is"
msgstr ""

msgid "``command(id, fn)``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Binds a command declared in the envelope to its function (also as a "
"decorator, ``@ctx.command(\"…\")``). A command not declared is refused."
msgstr ""

msgid "``on(event, fn)``, ``expose(name, obj)``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Listens to an event; makes a function available in the console as "
"``em.ext.<id>.<name>``."
msgstr ""

msgid "``file(name, content, mime)``"
msgstr ""

msgid "The file an exporter returns."
msgstr ""

msgid "``stamp(file, inputs=…, parameters=…, dtc_kind=…, technique=…)``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The stamp of a file the plugin made (API 1.2, see :doc:`stamp-derived-"
"files`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "``data_dir``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The plugin's own folder, ``~/.s3dgraphy/plugins-data/<id>/``, kept across"
" updates."
msgstr ""

msgid "``package``"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The data of the same archive (a mixed package): ``landmark_set(id)``, "
"``extractor_types``, ``combiner_types``, ``qualia_types``, "
"``label(type_id, lang)``; ``None`` for a plugin alone."
msgstr ""

msgid "``id``, ``version``, ``host``, ``verified``"
msgstr ""

msgid "Who the plugin is, where it runs, whether a review covers it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``teardown(ctx)``, when the object has it, runs when the plugin is turned"
" off."
msgstr ""

msgid "Errors"
msgstr ""

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"A function refuses with ``em.EmError({\"en\": \"…\", \"it\": \"…\"})``: "
"the command fails with the sentence in the language of the interface, and"
" EMStudio stays up. Any other exception is caught and said the same way. "
"A write the contract refuses raises ``em.Refused``; a feature the host "
"lacks, ``em.NotAvailable``; a node not found, ``em.NodeNotFound``."
msgstr ""

msgid "On the command line"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"``em.open(path)`` opens a study, ``em.use(graph, author=…)`` works on a "
"graph in memory with an author for its writes, ``em.save(path)`` writes "
"it. With ``s3dgraphy.em.plugins``, ``sync(host, dev=True)``, "
"``invoke(plugin, command, slots)`` and ``compute(items)`` load and run "
"the plugins as EMStudio does (see :doc:`test-and-validate`)."
msgstr ""

